      "writtenOn": "2019-03-15T09:19:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, it would not be correct to call it \u0027remote_id\u0027. \u0027remote_id\u0027 would refer to the IdP\u0027s entity ID, like \u0027https://samltest.id/idp\u0027. \u0027remote_id_attribute\u0027 is not that, rather it\u0027s the Apache header that is set by the SP module that indicates where keystone should *look for* the remote ID, for example \u0027Shib-Identity-Provider\u0027 or \u0027MELLON_IDP\u0027. \u0027remote_id_attribute\u0027 also mirrors the keystone.conf option that this is replacing.",
